From cd031daa391e9500df6e3c1fc4b47d7aeea20884 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NEMO executor <executor@nemo.local>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 11:26:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] coag: split Part C figures (L1 comparison + NEMO-vs-DustPy)

- plot_compare_dustpy.py: standalone plotter reading coag_dustpy_data/*.tsv (no
  NEMO/DustPy re-run), producing two figures:
    coag_dustpy_l1.*        L&L-style L1(code vs exact) vs dimensionless time,
                            both kernels -- comparable error, quantitative.
    coag_nemo_vs_dustpy.*   distributions overlaid (NEMO o, DustPy x, exact line),
                            both kernels -- 'two codes, same answer' for the
                            broad community.
- compare_dustpy.py now dump-only (plotting split out, matching Part B pattern).
- drop the old combined coag_dustpy_comparison.* figure.
